From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:45:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Keyboard & input homepage row, Sable Tools links and
 key hint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The approved Settings design has a top-level "Keyboard & input" row,
Diagnostics under it (not under Settings > Sable, which holds Sable
Setup only), "Privacy & security" and a keyboard hint footer.

* Homepage row "Keyboard & input" (Physical keyboard, typing) opens
  Android's keyboard page (KeyboardSettings), which already holds
  Physical keyboard, On-screen keyboard and the Keyboard light info row;
  Physical keyboard now comes first. Same page as System > Keyboard.
* The page gets "Tests and diagnostics": Typing test opens Sable Tools'
  critical text-entry test (OPEN_TOOL, TEXT_ENTRY) and Diagnostics opens
  Sable Tools, which lists only supported tools and keeps the 3377
  factory-test bridge behind its own gate. Both resolve to an explicit
  component in org.sableos.tools and are hidden and unindexed without
  it. Search aliases: diagnostics, factory test, 3377, key test, kb
  light, trackpad, mtklog (kb light also finds Keyboard light).
* Homepage type-ahead words for the new row; "keyboard" leaves System.
* The Safety Center homepage row is titled "Privacy & security".
* Homepage footer "↑↓ focus · Enter open · / search", not focusable,
  not indexed, shown only with a hardware QWERTY keyboard.
